# Markup and accessibility

Use semantic HTML elements that match the document structure already in the repo.
Do not invent a new heading order or landmark pattern in a single file.

Never put secrets, tokens, or credentials in HTML comments, data attributes, or
inline scripts.

Prefer existing design tokens, CSS variables, and shared classes over one-off
colors or spacing. Do not invent a CSS architecture the project does not already
use.

Fix layout in the same stylesheet layer the file already belongs to (global,
module, or utility). Do not introduce a new preprocessor or CSS-in-JS library
when the repo already has one.
